    "summary": "FFmpeg versions 8.0 through 8.1.2 contains a stack buffer overflow vulnerability in the Vulkan...",
    "details": "FFmpeg versions 8.0 through 8.1.2 contains a stack buffer overflow vulnerability in the Vulkan HEVC hardware decoder that allows remote attackers to overwrite return addresses and adjacent stack frames by supplying a crafted `HEVC/H.265` bitstream. Attackers can embed a malicious `vps_num_hrd_parameters` value exceeding `HEVC_MAX_SUB_LAYERS` in any supported container format to overflow stack-allocated arrays in the `vk_hevc_end_frame` function, potentially achieving arbitrary code execution.",
    "severity": [
